  "notes": "An i-adjective formed from {頼|たよ}り (reliance) + ない (not). Literally \"not reliable.\"\n\nFORMS:\n- Adverbial: {頼|たよ}りなく\n- Noun form: {頼|たよ}りなさ\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {頼|たよ}りない{人|ひと}: an unreliable person\n- {頼|たよ}りない{返事|へんじ}: a vague/uncertain reply\n- {頼|たよ}りなく{見|み}える: to look unreliable\n- {頼|たよ}りない{足取|あしど}り: unsteady steps\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {頼|たよ}もしい: reliable, reassuring, dependable (opposite)\n- {頼|たよ}りになる: to be someone you can count on\n- {頼|たよ}りない: undependable, inspiring no confidence\n\nUSAGE:\nOften used to describe people who seem inexperienced or lacking confidence, not necessarily those who break promises.",
